TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c05","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"checksum":"1babb77d1e6ab40fb9eb37a71d8d338c6ada6350f39a64d73fbe9955059a7d9a","id":"C1","kind":"claim","label":"Tightest dictionary (exact algebra, derived)","note":"prime-sum = 2·Cg·Re[ Σ_{p,k} (log p) p^{−k(1/2+iT0)} e^{−w²(k log p)²/2} ] = 2·Cg·Re[ windowed E₁(1/2,T0) ], our D8 energy E₁ = −ζ′/ζ, Gaussian-windowed in log(p^k), evaluated at σ=1/2. The window buys the convergence D8 could not have at σ=1/2 (needed σ>1 unwindowed). Step-2's cancellatory positivity and D8's termwise positivity are two faces: windowed vs unwindowed.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"6c2ca0504b94227625a7b6b7688d3ddb76b53b8f23545826ede33255d51f2e70","id":"C2","kind":"claim","label":"Uncertainty-principle load limit (exact, derived)","note":"Figure of merit is concentration: leakage 0.68 → 0.30 → 0.0007 as w = 2 → 1 → 0.5. Price: envelope e^{−w²u²/2} reaches 1e-12 at n = e^{7.4/w}: w=2 → 41, w=1 → 1700, w=0.5 → 2.8e6. No finite optimum — a Pareto frontier. Sharper zero-vision costs exponentially more prime data.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"93ac2f9cb63e88bfc9ea00d1d29139bd07c6cfaa8fd66a04b5845ecccd0fd9cf","id":"C3","kind":"claim","label":"S₁ is archimedean (structural, exact)","note":"Σ_{|γ|≤319} 1/ρ → 0.0230957 = 1 + γ/2 − (1/2)log(4π). Proof uses only the functional equation: S₁ = ξ′(1)/ξ(1) = [1 from s(s−1)] + [γ from zeta's Laurent] + [−(1/2)log π − log 2 from Gamma]. The prime Dirichlet series ΣΛ(n)n^{−s} diverges at s=1 — it never appears as a convergent sum. S₁ admits no convergent prime-sum presentation; its value is fixed by archimedean constants.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"b5b34276130304cad1677f48a53180c4791d734249d0ec50c5c45bd8eba9847c","id":"C4","kind":"claim","label":"Li as the inadmissible sharp limit of Weil (formal coda)","note":"λ_n is Weil-type positivity for the non-decaying 'test function' 1−((ρ−1)/ρ)^n — the sharp cutoff is exactly why its prime side diverges; Li is the inadmissible sharp limit of Weil.","status":"heuristic","type":"C"},{"checksum":"8411965ded1a5148a2f394aec81fbbe39b5c1309bb2e99728917ffaa04aed44d","id":"C5","kind":"claim","label":"The sieve's optimal quadratic form is inclusion-exclusion","note":"(Mμ)_S = Σ_T μ(T)/prod(S∪T) = δ_{S,∅}·δ(z) — the Möbius weights are the energy minimizers, and the minimum recovers the Mertens product exactly (not just asymptotically).","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"2ca3350680e3b36ef9d67e651070e15be4affd01a48e3f7c65221864fb0bc08f","generates":[{"prescription":"choose window (T0, w); form the even bump h(r) = e^{-(r-T0)²/2w²} + e^{-(r+T0)²/2w²} (sum of squares, ≥ 0, peak 1) and its exact Fourier partner g(u) = w√(2/π)·e^{−w²u²/2}·cos(T0·u)","stage":"detector"},{"prescription":"compute W(h) from the prime side only (80 zeros / 1.27M prime powers to 2e7) and read the derived bound N₊(B₊) ≤ e^{1/2}·W(h) on B₊ = [T0−w, T0+w]","stage":"windowed count"},{"prescription":"decompose components (pole / archimedean / prime-sum): a zero in the window drives the oscillatory prime sum negative, adding to W — the primes 'ring' at the zero's frequency; pole is exactly 0 for detectors (e^{−T0²/2w²})","stage":"resonance check"}],"honest_boundary":"The detector bound uses h ≥ 0 at the zeros, i.e. γ real — certified numerically per-window here (agreement to 1e-15 is the certificate), not proved in general. The bound is loose when zeros sit at the window edge — concentration relative to actual zero positions is what matters. Weil's criterion is cited, not derived.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D1","note":"Primes alone count zeros in a window: the bridge working as an instrument. Tighter windows leak less (0.68 → 0.30 → 0.0007) but cost exponentially more prime data — the uncertainty principle is the bridge's load limit in detector form.","rule":"Derived bound (h ≥ 0 + Weil formula): N₊(B₊) ≤ e^{1/2}·W(h), W(h) computed prime-side;  B₊ = [T0−w, T0+w].","subtitle":"D10a-step3 — the prime-side zero detector; resolution priced by uncertainty","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"W prime-side vs zero-side","expected":"T0=50, w=2: W′=3.8861, N₊=2, bound 6.41, leakage 0.6827; w=1: 2.2472, N₊=1, bound 3.71, leakage 0.2977; w=0.5: 1.8062, N₊=1, bound 2.98, leakage 0.0007; T0=100, w=2: 3.9959, N₊=2, bound 6.59, leakage 0.7001; T0=100, w=1: 1.8518, N₊=0, bound 3.05, leakage 1.8518 (zeros at 98.83/101.32 just outside)"},{"check":"agreement","expected":"4e-16 (8e-13 at w=0.5)"},{"check":"resonance components, T0=50","expected":"w=1.0: pole 0 + arch +1.6548 − (prime-sum −0.5925) = 2.2472; w=0.5: pole 0 + arch +0.8274 − (prime-sum −0.9788) = 1.8062; window empty (T0=100, w=1): prime-sum +0.3562, W all leakage"}]},{"checksum":"786ec5e107f962203903d357fe2b328523eeaef71b7a02a9e749e63e33475b53","generates":[{"prescription":"compute λ_n by Keiper–Taylor: L(w) = log ξ(1+w) series (Stieltjes numbers to k=40, polygamma at 1/2), formal log + composition with w = z/(1−z); λ_n = n[z^n]log ξ(1/(1−z))","stage":"A — exact, no zeros"},{"prescription":"compare against 2Re Σ_{0<γ≤319}[1−(1−1/ρ)^n] (150 zeros) and reconcile residuals with the zero-density tail integral","stage":"B — zero side"},{"prescription":"decompose S₁ = ξ′(1)/ξ(1) by source: [1 from s(s−1)] + [γ from zeta's Laurent] + [−(1/2)log π − log 2 from Gamma]","stage":"C — S₁ is archimedean"},{"prescription":"measure A_k(X,ε) = Σ_{n≤X} Λ(n)(log n)^k n^{−1−ε} growth vs k!/ε^{k+1}","stage":"D — obstruction"}],"honest_boundary":"Li's criterion (RH ⟺ λ_n ≥ 0, Li 1997) is cited, not derived. The Λ-sums that 'want' to be λ_n's coefficients diverge; λ_n needs their finite parts (η_k / Stieltjes constants) — renormalization, not direct summation. S₁ admits no convergent prime-sum presentation; its value is fixed by archimedean constants.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D2","note":"by contrasting presentations: Weil is face-sum-native (convergent windowed prime sums, 10a); Li is Dirichlet-series-native (finite parts of divergent sums). λ_n = Σ_{k=1}^n (−1)^{k+1}C(n,k)S_k is a coefficient positivity on the Dirichlet side — the face-sum reaches it only through renormalized divergent sums.","rule":"Li 1997 (cited): RH ⟺ λ_n ≥ 0 for all n ≥ 1,  λ_n = Σ_ρ[1 − (1−1/ρ)^n];  Keiper–Taylor: λ_n = n[z^n]log ξ(1/(1−z)).","subtitle":"D10b — Li's criterion through the D1 face-sum","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"Part A: n = 1..40","expected":"all λ_n ≥ 0 (min 0.0230957 at n=1); λ_1 = 0.0230957090, λ_2 = 0.0923457352 (match known values); λ_n/(n log n) = 0.067, 0.063, 0.072, 0.099, 0.146, 0.182, 0.207 (n=2..40) — rising toward the known (1/2)n log n asymptote"},{"check":"Part B: zero side (150 zeros) vs Taylor","expected":"n=1: 0.020642 vs 0.023096; n=10: 2.034 vs 2.279; n=30: 16.35 vs 18.55; tail estimated by the zero-density integral matches every observed gap to 3 s.f. (n=30: est 2.21, obs 2.21)"},{"check":"Part D: A_k(X,ε) growth","expected":"k=0: 7.45 → 10.50 (ε 0.10 → 0.05); k=1: 30.7 → 47.7; k=2: 98.0 → 156.2 — tracking k!/ε^{k+1} up to X-truncation"},{"check":"bug audit","expected":"zero-side sums initially missed the ρ↔ρ̄ doubling; caught by the n=1 mismatch, fixed"}]},{"checksum":"1338eb187703fd621367678179b95bf2451eb90f43ed7ef03f198c23ccb6dbf7","generates":[{"prescription":"form M_{S,T} = 1/prod(S∪T) on the finite complex Δ_z (primes ≤ z, squarefree d ↔ face S, lcm = prod of union), λ_∅ = 1","stage":"face-native form"},{"prescription":"verify M positive definite (Cholesky + all eigenvalues > 0, z ≤ 19); write Q(λ) = Σ_k w_k (v_k·λ)² via M's eigendecomposition (not M^{−1}'s)","stage":"sum of squares"},{"prescription":"split (Mμ)_S: prod(S∪T) = prod S · prod(T\\S); disjoint split T = T1∪T2 gives (1/prod S)·[(1−1)^{|S|} = δ_{S,∅}]·[Σ_{T2∩S=∅} μ(T2)/prod T2 = δ(z) at S=∅] — Mμ = δ(z)e_∅, so λ*_S = μ(S), Qmin = δ(z)","stage":"Möbius inversion (exact)"},{"prescription":"compare Qmin = δ(19) = 0.1710 against classical level-truncated 1/G(19) = 0.2348","stage":"classical comparison"}],"honest_boundary":"Selberg's form is an upper-bound machine: PD by construction (positivity assumed, not discovered from arithmetic), no analytic continuation, no zeros — and the parity barrier stands: the same form bounds primes and almost-primes alike, so no amount of optimization resolves ω(n) parity. 10c gives the template, not an independent zero-detecting positivity source; that remains 10d.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D3","note":"via Möbius inversion on the face-union incidence: the sieve's optimal quadratic form is inclusion-exclusion — the Möbius weights are the energy minimizers, and the minimum recovers the Mertens product exactly (not just asymptotically).","rule":"Q(λ) = Σ_{S,T} λ_S λ_T / prod(S∪T),  λ_∅ = 1;  M_{S,T} = 1/prod(S∪T) positive definite;  optimizer λ*_S = μ(S),  Qmin = δ(z) = ∏_{p≤z}(1−1/p).","subtitle":"D10c — Selberg's λ² sieve as an optimized quadratic form","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"optimizer + minimum, z ≤ 19","expected":"Qmin/δ(z) = 1 to 12 digits; max|λ*−μ| < 5e-14"},{"check":"PD","expected":"Cholesky + all eigenvalues > 0 verified z ≤ 19 (min eig 1.1e-8 at z=19)"},{"check":"classical comparison","expected":"1/G(19) = 0.2348 vs face-native Qmin = δ(19) = 0.1710; the d ≤ z truncation is a constraint; the full-face optimum is the better (smaller) bound; both → e^{−γ}/log z asymptotically"},{"check":"bug audit","expected":"square reconstruction must use M's eigendecomposition, not M^{−1}'s — caught and fixed"}]},{"checksum":"c4b758067f364f80a53a57fdae2daf4a05f9f53ca9d633e104b8e2e1ffeb73c7","from":"C1","id":"L1","rel":"defines","to":"D1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"01d3339f43fed9d7b6484e8a8f8e3673cb66bf62cddc7a08ba624e1fe0c11db6","from":"C2","id":"L2","rel":"bounds","to":"D1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"52fb7a5fb122c7c78106e742db2f3f2d6244247b31540923d62ea215559af9c9","from":"C3","id":"L3","rel":"supports","to":"D2","type":"L"},{"checksum":"535d644dfc414a2604467c5b04521eea5504e70f4f300b177c433eb5ffa6897d","from":"D3","id":"L4","rel":"exemplifies","to":"V2","type":"L"},{"checksum":"810aeb14894f1671b824b5f5acae50b8c01eec6f2b4d45d13b4ba20cc6c260d9","from":"V2","id":"L5","rel":"implements","to":"V3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"0355fad66f576593d979db03e8d90232566abd26815d512fd9121072aba37290","from":"C4","id":"L6","rel":"refines","to":"D2","type":"L"},{"checksum":"2109ce7453449e85965dc1958733862a959767cfd29acacf5c18ad60a403ebe4","consequence":"10a complete: the formula now runs entirely on our objects — grounded (step 1), positivity structured (step 2), detector built and priced (step 3). The remaining open span — an independent Gram/intersection source for the positivity — belongs to the whole bridge program (10d its natural home), not to translation.","id":"V1","status":"exact","subject":"10a span","type":"V"},{"checksum":"b314cd5907c6bca2042a6bb834517e75f2d00d6ac6126f65b69c3ffab6a1d5ec","consequence":"The face-sum's native positivity is Weil-type (smoothed/windowed); do not expect it to carry coefficient-positivity directly. Sharpens the hunt: 10c (Selberg λ², a genuine quadratic form) and 10d (function-field template) are where an independent source can live.","id":"V2","status":"exact","subject":"10b — Li vs face-sum","type":"V"},{"checksum":"fbad04a7d4e635b41786f90eb227020cc29c6b53a10a20884990345726ca4b36","consequence":"Selberg's form is the canonical optimized quadratic form on the complex: finite, convergent, Weil-type (sum of squares) — consistent with 10b's lesson that the face-sum carries Weil-type, not Li-type, positivity. It is the template, not an independent zero-detecting positivity source; that remains 10d.","id":"V3","status":"exact","subject":"10c — Selberg λ² form","type":"V"}],"registry":{"C1":"C","C2":"C","C3":"C","C4":"C","C5":"C","D1":"D","D2":"D","D3":"D","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","L4":"L","L5":"L","L6":"L","V1":"V","V2":"V","V3":"V"},"wire_checksum":"10dff5a89fb889833d84cc7e608d9e5c622aa1f881fc47526dfe7b35a415a0e2"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1